<figure class="diagram metadata-resolution">
  <p class="metadata-question"><b>Input:</b> A Sunken record identifies a route
  such as <code>Auth/2</code>. Service dispatch maps that route to a top-level
  type in the embedded BSN metadata.</p>

  <div class="metadata-flow" aria-label="Five stages from a Sunken route to a named payload schema">
    <div class="metadata-step metadata-route"
      aria-label="Step one: read direction, slot zero, and command two">
      <span>1</span><strong>Wire route</strong><small><code>S→C slot 0 / command 2</code></small>
    </div>
    <i aria-hidden="true">→</i>
    <div class="metadata-step metadata-dispatch"
      aria-label="Step two: static service dispatch labels the route Auth slash two and selects the generated payload decoder">
      <span>2</span><strong>Static dispatch</strong><small><code>Auth/2</code> + handler</small>
    </div>
    <i aria-hidden="true">→</i>
    <div class="metadata-step metadata-type-id"
      aria-label="Step three: the handler is associated with a numeric top-level type identifier">
      <span>3</span><strong>Top-level type ID</strong><small>symbolically: <code>T</code></small>
    </div>
    <i aria-hidden="true">→</i>
    <div class="metadata-step metadata-records"
      aria-label="Step four: type T selects a structural record and an optional naming record">
      <span>4</span><strong>Metadata entry <code>T</code></strong>
      <small>shape + optional names</small>
    </div>
    <i aria-hidden="true">→</i>
    <div class="metadata-step metadata-schema"
      aria-label="Step five: recursively resolving child type identifiers produces a readable schema">
      <span>5</span><strong>Readable schema</strong>
      <small><code>Authentication::ProofRequest</code></small>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="metadata-entry-pair" aria-label="The two records associated with a BSN type identifier">
    <div>
      <strong>Structural record</strong>
      <span>kind, bounds, flags, and child type IDs</span>
    </div>
    <b aria-hidden="true">+</b>
    <div>
      <strong>Naming record</strong>
      <span>type name, member names, enum and choice labels</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="metadata-explainer">
    <p class="metadata-default"><b>Route numbers and type IDs occupy separate
    namespaces.</b> Dispatch maps the route to generated code and a top-level
    payload type. Metadata defines that type and its child types.</p>
  </div>
</figure>
